      "description": "Watch Motherwell vs HJK helsinki highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 13, 2026. The stage was set for a high-stakes encounter as Motherwell and HJK Helsinki went head-to-head in a crucial UEFA Conference League fixture. Both sides took to the pitch on August 13, 2026 , looking to secure a vital advantage in their continental campaign. A Tactical Battle in the Opening Period The first half was characterized by a cautious approach from both teams, with much of the action contested in a crowded midfield. Motherwell attempted to find gaps in the opposition defense, but the visitors remained disciplined and organized. The intensity of the match was evident as challenges flew in, leading to the game's first booking in the 43rd minute when Alfie Cicale received a yellow card. Despite the effort from both camps, clear-cut chances were at a premium, and the referee blew for half-time with the deadlock still unbroken. Ibrahim Said Takes Center Stage The dynamic of the match shifted dramatically immediately after the restart. In the 47th minute, HJK Helsinki surged ahead as Ibrahim Said clinical finish found the back of the net to break the stalemate. The visitors grew in confidence, and despite Alexander Ring picking up a yellow card in the 57th minute, their momentum remained unchecked. Just three minutes later, Ibrahim Said struck again in the 60th minute, doubling his tally and putting his side in a commanding position as the home crowd watched on in frustration. Strategic Changes and the Final Whistle As the clock ticked down, both managers turned to their benches to inject fresh energy into the game. HJK Helsinki introduced the experienced Teemu Pukki and Mouhamed Gueye , while Motherwell looked to the likes of Ewan Wilson and Mikey Booth to spark a late comeback. A flurry of substitutions in the 68th minute saw Martin Kirilov and Till Cissokho enter the fray, but the visitors' defensive structure held firm against any late pressure. After four minutes of stoppage time, the final whistle confirmed a decisive result for the Finnish side, fueled by Said's match-winning performance."
